'''Kel Dors''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Dorin]]. In order to survive [[oxygen]]-rich environments, they wore [[Antiox breath mask|specialized]] [[breath mask]]s that covered their [[eye]]s and nostrils.<ref name="SWJB" /> [[Jedi Master]] [[Plo Koon]] was a Kel Dor who served on the [[Jedi High Council|Jedi Council]] in the last [[Standard year|years]] of the [[Jedi Order]] and the [[Galactic Republic]]. [[Bo Keevil]] was also a member of the species, who served as a [[pilot]] in [[Ace Squadron]].<ref name="Bo Keevil" />

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:Steadfast-WotF.png|thumb|left|200px|right|Kel Dor physiology allowed them to temporarily survive the vacuum of space.]]
The Kel Dor were a tall, [[humanoid]] [[species]] that possessed three [[Limb|fingers]] and a thumb on each hand.<ref name="Rising ''Malevolence''">{{TCW|Rising Malevolence|Rising ''Malevolence''}}</ref> The thick,<ref name="Updated and Expanded">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> [[leather]]y<ref name="Plo Koon DB">{{Databank|plo-koon|Plo Koon}}</ref> hide<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> that covered their bodies allowed them to survive exposure to the [[vacuum]] of [[Realspace|space]] for a [[time]].<ref name="Plo Koon DB" /> The Kel Dor wore [[Antiox breath mask|masks]] to filter the air when they were offworld due to [[oxygen]] being [[poison]]ous to them. They also wore [[goggles]] to protect their eye fluids from evaporating.<ref name="Everything" /> Genetically, they were distantly related to the [[Gand]] and [[Tognath]] species, who similarly wore breath masks when offworld.<ref name="Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref>

==Society and culture==
Kel Dor society was made of clans. The [[antiox breath mask]]s that the Kel Dor wore were decorated with patterns that were unique to each clan.<ref name="Complete Visual Dictionary">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref>

Members of the species would greet each other with the phrase "Koh-to-yah!", which translated to "greetings!"<ref name="Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref>

The Kel Dor were directly represented in the [[Galactic Senate]]. Within the [[Imperial Senate Building|Senate Building]], the Kel Dor delegation occupied several rooms that were equipped so that antiox masks were unnecessary.<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

